+def block_bounds(n: int, world: int, rank: int, block: int = 128) -> tuple[int, int]:
+    """``rank``'s [lo, hi) of ``n`` elements split into whole ``block``-wide pieces: every rank gets
+    ``n // block // world`` blocks and the first ``(n // block) % world`` ranks one more. Even splits (every TP2
+    shape, and TP4 attention) are the plain equal parts; TP4 experts (2,304 = 18 blocks) are 640/640/512/512 and the
+    TP4 vocabulary (1,010 blocks) 32,384/32,384/32,256/32,256. Boundaries stay on whole Hadamard blocks (EXL3)."""
